{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788112102,"nonce":"99BFS3LpPJtVJaicCNQWGBTVrmE=","title":"3.4 Pawn orders + policies","message":"Wave 3 — hands. Depends: 1.1, 2.2 (pawn ids/fields), 2.4 (policies).\n\n## Goal\nPawn orders + colony management: draft-layer commands and the standing-policy\nlevers (work, schedule, outfits, food, drugs) — the clothes lever included.\n\n## Context (read first)\n- DESIGN.md §Action model; §Observation (upkeep layer — these verbs are what\n  the morning checklist pulls)\n- decompiled: Pawn_DraftController, Pawn_JobTracker.TryTakeOrderedJob +\n  JobGiver paths, FloatMenuMakerMap (what right-click offers = parity list),\n  WorkGiver scan for prioritize, Pawn_WorkSettings, Pawn_TimetableTracker,\n  OutfitDatabase + Pawn_OutfitTracker (+ food/drug equivalents), BillStack\n  (medical bills on pawns), HostilityResponseMode\n- MP sync registry (these are the most-synced verbs in existence)\n\n## Scope\n- Orders: draft/undraft, move-to P, attack thing, prioritize {job} on {thing}\n  (the right-click equivalent; validate via the WorkGiver), rescue/capture/\n  carry-to-bed, arrest, equip/wear/drop, consume (eat/take drug).\n- Management: work priorities get/set (matrix or per-pawn), schedule assign\n  (blocks), outfit/food/drug policy create/edit/assign, hostility response,\n  self-tend, medical care level, allowed area assign (2.3's areas),\n  medical bills: add/remove operation bills on a pawn.\n- Colony-level: `wardens interact` minimal prisoner ops (recruit toggle,\n  release) if cheap; else defer to a later wave and say so on the issue.\n\n## Invariants\nOrders go through the same code paths player clicks produce (TryTakeOrderedJob\netc.) so mods' patches see identical traffic; failures return the game's own\nreject reasons; policy edits journaled.\n\n## Open questions (worker's)\nPrioritize surface breadth v1 (haul/tend/repair/construct at minimum);\nschedule block format; policy spec format (mirror 3.2's filter approach).\n\n## Acceptance\n- Draft + move + undraft round-trip; drafted pawn holds position.\n- prioritize haul on a specific stack → that pawn hauls it next.\n- Outfit policy \"cold\" assigned → pawn re-dresses into warmer apparel under\n  advance (verifies the whole clothes loop end to end).\n- Surgery bill added → doctor performs it under advance on a fixture.","files":null}]}